<title>JAPAN: Thailand's Bangchak tenders to buy May crude.</title>
<headline>Thailand's Bangchak tenders to buy May crude.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Bangchak Petroleum Plc has tendered to buy 500,000 barrels of Middle East crude oil and 600,000 barrels of Far East crude oil for May loading, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes 6 p.m. local time (1100 GMT) on March 26, and offers should be valid until the same hour on March 27.</p>
<p>The Thai refiner traditionally favours buying Oman, and has been known to buy multiple cargoes of Oman in its tender.</p>
</text>
